Supplement after review
=======================

Command:
  PYTHONPATH="$PWD" /home/asa/devel/libresolid-studio/.venv/bin/python \
    -m pytest -q tests/test_flexible_cache_performance.py \
    tests/test_molejo_adapter.py::MolejoMeshPathPairTest \
    tests/test_flexible_node.py

Result: 42 passed, 2 existing legacy-render FutureWarnings in 5.88s.

The supplement adds a 128-distinct-structural-identity trajectory at the
default 64-entry cap and verifies revisit bounds/volume after eviction. It
also corrects a compatibility gap found in review: a public `base_mesh()`
override is used unchanged and uncached when its custom mesh cannot be proven
by the stock serialized-spec key. The coherent stock path still calls
`_snapshot_mesh(rendered, values)` exactly once per miss.
